<ui:UiBinder xmlns:ui="urn:ui:com.google.gwt.uibinder"
             xmlns:g="urn:import:com.google.gwt.user.client.ui"
             xmlns:d="urn:import:org.gwtbootstrap5.demo.client.ui">
    <g:HTMLPanel>
        <h1>Setup</h1>
        <p class="lead">Add the dependency, inherit the GWT module, and use the widgets from Java or UiBinder.</p>

        <h2 class="h4 mt-5">1. Add the dependency</h2>
        <p>GwtBootstrap5 is on Maven Central. It needs GWT 2.13 and Java 17.</p>
        <d:CodeBlock ui:field="dependency" language="xml"/>

        <h2 class="h4 mt-5">2. Inherit the GWT module</h2>
        <d:CodeBlock ui:field="inherits" language="xml"/>
        <p>Pick the module by where Bootstrap's files come from:</p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm align-middle">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Module</th><th>Bootstrap 5.3.8, Popper and Bootstrap Icons</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>org.gwtbootstrap5.GwtBootstrap5</code></td>
                        <td>Bundled in the jar and served with your app. The usual choice.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>org.gwtbootstrap5.GwtBootstrap5URL</code></td>
                        <td>Loaded from the jsDelivr CDN.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>org.gwtbootstrap5.GwtBootstrap5NoResources</code></td>
                        <td>Not loaded: your host page loads Bootstrap (and Popper, if an extra needs it) itself.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>If the page already has Bootstrap 5, GwtBootstrap5 doesn't load it again.</p>

        <h2 class="h4 mt-5">3. Write the host page</h2>
        <p>Bootstrap 5 needs the HTML5 doctype and the viewport meta tag for its responsive layout.</p>
        <d:CodeBlock ui:field="host" language="html"/>

        <h2 class="h4 mt-5">4. Use the widgets in UiBinder</h2>
        <p>
            Widgets are in <code>org.gwtbootstrap5.client.ui</code> and plain HTML elements as widgets in
            <code>org.gwtbootstrap5.client.ui.html</code>. The code shown in this demo uses the <code>b</code>,
            <code>b.html</code> and <code>g</code> prefixes below.
        </p>
        <d:CodeBlock ui:field="uiBinder" language="xml"/>

        <h2 class="h4 mt-5">5. Add the extras you need</h2>
        <p>
            The extras are a separate artifact, with one GWT module per extra. Most have <code>URL</code> and
            <code>NoResources</code> variants like the core module. <code>Select</code> and the date pickers load
            their engine separately: add its resources module (or its <code>URL</code> variant) too. The Extras pages
            of this demo show which modules each one needs.
        </p>
        <d:CodeBlock ui:field="extras" language="xml"/>

        <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Upgrading from 0.2.x or 0.1.x</h2>
        <p>
            0.3.0 removes the APIs deprecated in 0.2.x, and 0.2.0 changed the Maven <code>groupId</code> and several APIs. See
            <a href="https://github.com/gwtbootstrap5/gwtbootstrap5-parent/blob/master/UPGRADING.md">UPGRADING.md</a>
            for what to change.
        </p>
    </g:HTMLPanel>
</ui:UiBinder>
